// The child repos `yarn clone` puts inside the kit `spell-kit` (checked out at `~/www/spell`), each its own git repo
// (epic `repo-split` P7, Q15-Q17).
// - The kit itself is the bottom of every list, and always there:  every repo uses it (`spell-kit/util`,
//   `spell-kit/element` ...), so no `needs` names it (epic `repo-split` P9:  spell-util, spell-server and spell-element
//   are its folders now).
// - Lowest first:  a repo only ever uses the ones above it in this list ("Every arrow points down").
// - `needs`:  the repos its CODE uses, directly:  `yarn clone <repo>` clones those too, and theirs, and so on.
// - `runs`:  repos it runs by its settings, never imports (spell-app's page server runs spell-epic's route modules):
//   cloned with it too, but no arrow in the layout's picture.
// - `url`:  where `yarn clone` clones it from;  over SSH, falling back to HTTPS (GitHub's login, `gh auth`) when SSH is
//   refused.
// - Read by `tools/repos.ts` (`yarn clone`, `yarn pull`, `yarn status`, and the checks over every repo).
{
  "repos": [
    { "name": "spell-lang", "url": "git@github.com:spell-app/spell-lang.git", "needs": [] },
    { "name": "spell-ui", "url": "git@github.com:spell-app/spell-ui.git", "needs": [] },
    { "name": "spell-brand", "url": "git@github.com:spell-app/spell-brand.git", "needs": ["spell-ui"] },
    {
      "name": "spell-epic",
      "url": "git@github.com:spell-app/spell-epic.git",
      "needs": ["spell-brand", "spell-ui"]
    },
    {
      "name": "spell-app",
      "url": "git@github.com:spell-app/spell-app.git",
      "needs": ["spell-lang", "spell-brand", "spell-ui"],
      "runs": ["spell-epic"]
    }
  ]
}
